{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>As an adversary to him.</b> I have already explained it in the book of Job, that the satan was the angel. As for the words of the Gaon [Saadia], that it is a human being — they carry no weight."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The idiom לא מעלין ולא מורידין ('neither raises nor lowers') is rendered here in its standard sense of 'carries no weight' rather than a more literal translation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:54.878276374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}